Description: KDE Plasma applet to control MOONDROP Bluetooth headphones
 Noise cancelling modes, tuning presets, a five band parametric EQ, the
 LDAC/LC3/LHDC switches, DAC gain, multipoint and battery levels, all read
 and written over the headphone's RFCOMM control channel.
 .
 The applet talks to the headphone directly through an AF_BLUETOOTH socket as
 the ordinary user; it needs neither root nor bluetoothctl.
 .
 Verified on MOONDROP EDGE (firmware 1.4.0) and Moondrop Nekocake (firmware
 1.0.0).  Profiles for other models come from public protocol documentation
 and are shown as unverified in the user interface.
